    "created_at": "2018-11-15T04:04:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-11-15T04:04:01Z",
    "body": "We could update this, and add similar language to what #3829 did, but to **allowed to play** -- the wording in this PR doesn't match what we're using for feature policy anymore.\r\n\r\nI'm worried, though, that doing that would mean that the policy would disable JavaScript controls completely, since **allowed to play** is referenced from `.play()`. Is that what we want?\r\n\r\nMaybe **allowed to play** should reference **eligible for autoplay** somehow: If the document has not had any activation, and the element is not eligible for autoplay, then the element should not be allowed to play.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/438909764/reactions",
