    "created_at": "2018-11-15T16:31:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-11-15T16:31:28Z",
    "body": "The feature policy will allow an iframe to autoplay if the parent is\nallowed to autoplay. In other words, a main frame could get a user gesture\nand allow the child frame to play trough it.\n\nOn Wed., Nov. 14, 2018, 20:07 Domenic Denicola <notifications@github.com\nwrote:\n\n> Hmm. I'm unclear what the current implementation status is for things like\n> .play() and its ties to feature policy. E.g. if you set the\n> autoplay-allowed feature policy, does that mean the page can call play()\n> no matter what, in contemporary implementations? (Even without user\n> activation?)\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you were mentioned.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/3253#issuecomment-438910315>, or mute\n> the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAjAljC4Bs822_jBMoBuShRVF-y7l_bjks5uvOiNgaJpZM4Qomfi>\n> .\n>\n",
